{"id": "EUVD-2026-81788", "enisaUuid": "c814f166-f219-39c9-bd4c-2515a84be6ed", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nriscv, bpf: Fix missing sign-ext for signed 1-byte and 2-byte kfunc args\n\nOn RV64, the ABI requires sign-extension for signed 1-byte and 2-byte kfunc\nargs. However, the RV64 JIT currently does not perform sign-extension for\nsuch kfunc args.\n\nBefore commit 7ce090afbf72 (\"bpf: Infer zext_dst based on static register\nliveness analysis\"), state pruning could potentially omit zero-extension\nof 32-bit subregisters, which inadvertently masked the above issue by making\nthe args appear as if they had been properly sign-extended. After that\ncommit, the problem is exposed, causing the kfunc_call/kfunc_call_test4\nselftest to fail.\n\nFix this by extending the existing sign-extension logic to handle signed\n1-byte and 2-byte kfunc args as well.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:07:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:59:31", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/555fc6f1caf00ce7005e732b688da26c0dc3c5c5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/801ae90f8ce099187e6224cec7d72d07a4df0324", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/71dbd143be598954ae103feadd12692aeb0f2f88", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f2aaa621591093cfe8224a25ef2f04a3b1e304b0"], "aliases": ["GHSA-wm8w-4px2-2hp8", "CVE-2026-90195"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e3fdfe9-21a2-320c-97ee-620a2ce0428f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.52"}, {"id": "416356db-4a3c-3f0b-bf46-90480efd512b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "554c4aee-c807-3129-acce-c591dd2e7b6d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443574b033876c85a35de4c65c14f7fe092222b2 <71dbd143be598954ae103feadd12692aeb0f2f88"}, {"id": "63bd15b1-b9e4-325f-a3f0-5683c8aa563c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "6d04dbbd-6581-3089-8d02-c3afa11c9b58", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443574b033876c85a35de4c65c14f7fe092222b2 <f2aaa621591093cfe8224a25ef2f04a3b1e304b0"}, {"id": "6f972f0b-5a24-3c2b-948c-aaf8b432b20d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.110"}, {"id": "7273666a-7ee2-302b-b51d-8c2b3565e556", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443574b033876c85a35de4c65c14f7fe092222b2 <555fc6f1caf00ce7005e732b688da26c0dc3c5c5"}, {"id": "7c63fc3a-bd50-3bc0-aec0-a3b66413989a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "443574b033876c85a35de4c65c14f7fe092222b2 <801ae90f8ce099187e6224cec7d72d07a4df0324"}, {"id": "ae763e1d-9e0a-328e-97ce-3c160e66c727", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e8116c04-36e2-367a-b2b6-631eeae5a4a5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "db8a0e5c-eacf-3897-a121-8ee95070dad6", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}